{"diagnosis": "Fetch test with 256 NOPs traps with `TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000` vs expected advancing PC, yielding `tohost: FAIL 0xdead`. Every NOP (opcode 0010011, funct3 000) satisfies the wrong decode at picorv32.v:870 where `instr_jalr` uses `!= 7'b1100111` instead of `==`. The false JALR with rs1=x0 and imm=0 forces jump target 0x0, pinning PC at 0 and preventing progress.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -867,7 +867,7 @@
 			instr_lui     <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110111;
 			instr_auipc   <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010111;
 			instr_jal     <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1101111;
-			instr_jalr    <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] != 7'b1100111 && mem_rdata_latched[14:12] == 3'b000;
+			instr_jalr    <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1100111 && mem_rdata_latched[14:12] == 3'b000;
 			instr_retirq  <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0001011 && mem_rdata_latched[31:25] == 7'b0000010 && ENABLE_IRQ;
 			instr_waitirq <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0001011 && mem_rdata_latched[31:25] == 7'b0000100 && ENABLE_IRQ;
", "expected": "tohost PASS with progress max_addr > 0x00000000 and no TRAP: no progress"}

